                "description": "Which part of the parent work this variant shows. Meaningful for role='partial-crop', where a wide painting is split into complementary crops. Tintoretto's Miracle of the Loaves and Fishes (Met 13.75) is 154.9 x 407.7 cm — aspect 2.63 — so no 16:9 panel can hold it; a left and a right crop together show what one crop cannot."
