    "derived_from": {
      "type": [
        "object",
        "null"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Set when this entry is a SECTION of another work presented in its own right — a detail crop of a fresco, a reconstruction, a distinct state of a print. A detail is genuinely presentable but has no independent identity: it inherits the parent's. This is deliberately NOT `files.variants[]`, which models device fitness (tv-master, meural-framed, thumbnail) rather than curatorial selection.\n\nINVARIANT: a sidecar with `derived_from` set MUST have `stable_identifiers.wikidata_q` null. Giving details work-level identity is how one Q-ID (Q547923, 'The Raising of Lazarus') came to sit on 50 distinct Scrovegni sidecars. Enforced by the `derived_identity` audit check.",
      "properties": {
        "work_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "work_id of the parent this is a section of."
        },
        "region": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "description": "Where in the parent, as 'x,y,w,h' in parent pixel coordinates when known, otherwise a human description ('with Hell')."
        },
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "detail",
            "reconstruction",
            "state",
            "capture"
          ],
          "description": "detail = a section shown separately; capture = another photograph of the same element; reconstruction/state = derived renderings."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "work_id",
        "kind"
      ]
    },
    "existence": {
      "type": [
        "object",
        "null"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Whether the work still physically exists. Every other class in this archive assumes permanence — a painting in a museum, a fresco in a chapel. Street art does not: a mural dated 2012-2014 may have been painted over, and then the capture in this archive is not a reproduction of a surviving object but the only surviving record of it. Absent for works where permanence is a safe assumption.",
      "properties": {
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "extant",
            "overpainted",
            "demolished",
            "removed",
            "unknown"
          ]
        },
        "as_of": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "description": "When the status was last established."
        },
        "note": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "status"
      ]
    },
    "identity_anchor": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "enum": [
        "artist",
        "place",
        "capture",
        null
      ],
      "description": "Which fact carries this record's identity, recorded because for some classes it is not the usual one. The archive normally identifies a work by its own Wikidata item; where none exists the anchor falls through in precedence order:\n  artist  - a resolvable maker (Q-ID preferred, name accepted)\n  place   - coordinates or a named location; a wall has no Q-ID and\n            that is not a gap to be filled\n  capture - the photograph IS the record, with `existence` saying\n            whether the subject survives\nEach level is used when the one above is unavailable, and the levels combine: recording the anchor does not stop the other fields being populated when they are known."
    }
  },
  "allOf": [
    {
      "$comment": "A derived item inherits identity from its parent, so it must not assert a work Q-ID of its own. Enforced HERE rather than in each writer because sidecar.write() validates on every write, so every pass gets it for free and none can reintroduce it. Prose alone did not hold: the invariant was documented in derived_from's own description while Q547923 spread across 50 Scrovegni sidecars, and on 2026-08-09 a pass rewrote a cleared value back onto the Birth of Venus crop twice in one day.",
      "if": {
        "required": [
          "derived_from"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "derived_from": {
            "type": "object"
          }
        }
      },
      "then": {
        "required": [
          "stable_identifiers"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "stable_identifiers": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "wikidata_q"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "wikidata_q": {
                "const": null
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
